WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.710
In 1993, Jensen Huang co-founded NVIDIA

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.010
to build graphics chips for video games.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.320
Today, AI is everywhere.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.980
Even an 80-year-old retiree uses it.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.100
And AI runs on GPUs — the chips built for games —

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.670
doing thousands of calculations at once.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:22.110
NVIDIA is a leading supplier of AI chips for data centers.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.980
Quarterly revenue: $68.1 billion,

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.700
then $81.6 billion, then $96.2 billion.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.530
Major partners, and earnings ahead: the next catalyst.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.840
Picture the stock rising 8%,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.880
from $218 to $235.44.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.840
By investing $25,000 with about 5× leverage,

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.630
you could potentially make $9,975.68 — before costs.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:53.160
At $50,000 and 7.5×: nearly $30,000.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:57.050
Hypothetical. Leverage magnifies losses too.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.690
Not guaranteed. Not financial advice.
